			<div class="content" id="post-content-4829967">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Currently unknown. Not sure what to categorize this SCP's genre.</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Image, containment procedures, description, diary/interviews/addenda</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> 2 anomalous entities designated SCP-XXXX-A and B. XXXX-A is a middle-aged woman living inside the house, who can summon any object upon request, usually in a similar manner to &quot;Mom, can you find XYZ for me?&quot;. XXXX-B is a house, in which objects not belonging to direct family members (children and significant other) placed in it vanish after a couple hours.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> (will be told from a first person perspective of XXXX-A, from a diary, as well as interviews with Foundation personnel) The woman first discovers her powers on accident, and over the course of a couple years, discovers both the extent and limitations of her anomalous abilities, such as basis on her emotional state, as well as trying to explore the limit of the alternate dimension from which she can summon objects. The diary follows the woman's (Claudia) life as she begins to adapt to being an anomaly, as well as being introduced to the Foundation, with whom Claudia cooperates with willingly, but under certain rules: she must keep her children and husband, and her day-to-day life must not be interrupted constantly; in return, she performs tests with the Foundation, and consents to being amnesticized after tests, in order to not spread Foundation information.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> XXXX-A summoned human leg bones covered in old, decayed flesh, as well as an unknown fluid, according to a police interview with a burglar.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I want to use the addendum section to insert XXXX-A's diary, but also slip in some references to the woman's background in the description. This SCP is a darker version of the cliche &quot;Mom, I can't find XYZ&quot; and your mom is the only one who can find the object in the house. I have made some changes here in this post as requested by Savanac from IRC.</p>

