<p>Hi! Thanks for the crit.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I totally understand what you mean. I spent a couple days on IRC asking around for some help on this piece, and people kept telling me that it needed either more story, more of a personal connection with XXXX-A (because she's human), or both. I tried to do both, but I am <em>really</em> bad at explaining things.</p>
<p>My goal isn't to entirely tell the story of the SCP just using the first person, where XXXX-A is speaking the entire time; rather, I want to write in the first person to evolve XXXX-A as more than just 'one more SCP to contain', and give XXXX-A a bit of personality and connection.</p>
<p>My goal for the tests she performs with the Foundation are SCP-XXXX specific, and with Foundation goals in mind, such as how can XXXX-A's abilities be exploited to benefit the Foundation (can she summon things that can provide energy? Can she summon weapons? Foundation-critical resources?)</p>
<p>Additionally, I didn't want to really make this SCP one full of conflict, but I do agree that there should be more tension. I wanted to portray a softer side of the Foundation, in which this SCP cooperates with the Foundation, and they don't enforce harsh containment restrictions upon her because of her attitude towards the Foundation.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

